<title>USA: U.S. March personal income rose 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. March personal income rose 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  March    Feb--(Prev)   Jan--(Prev)   Dec</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.6    0.8    0.9    0.3    0.4    0.7</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.6    0.8    0.8    0.7    0.7    0.7</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.5    0.5    0.6    0.6    0.6    0.5</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.5    0.5    0.3    1.2    1.0    0.4</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.4    0.2    0.1    1.1    0.9    0.2</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: March    Feb--(Prev)   Jan--(Prev)   Dec</p>
<p> Income		   6,745  6,706  6,713  6,653  6,655  6,629</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,851  5,818  5,825  5,774  5,777  5,735</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,541  5,516  5,503  5,490  5,484  5,428</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,371  5,346  5,334  5,322  5,316  5,261</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   664    660    652    659    652    637</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,607  1,601  1,596  1,593  1,590  1,571</p>
<p> -Services		3,100  3,085  3,086  3,070  3,074  3,053</p>
<p> Personal Savings	 310    302    322    284    293    307</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.3    5.2    5.5    4.9    5.1    5.3</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,827  3,800  3,801  3,751  3,751  3,753</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   699    693    692    689    689    692</p>
<p> -Service Industries  1,354  1,341  1,341  1,317  1,316  1,320</p>
<p> -Government		659    657    658    654    654    647</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    552    550    537    545    535    542</p>
<p> -Farm			 45     45     45     46     47     46</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  507    504    492    499    488    495</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected March personal income to rise 0.4 percent and spending to be up 0.5 percent.</p>
